# synth.ys — Yosys synthesis script for release_logic.v
# Produces a NAND-only netlist (TapeOut processors are built from NAND
# gates and LATCHes), written to release_logic_netlist.v.
#
# Run:
#     yosys synth.ys
#
# Route: `abc -g NAND` maps the design to $_NAND_ / $_NOT_ internal cells.
# Yosys `write_verilog` renders those cells as continuous assignments
# (`assign Y = ~(A & B);` / `assign Y = ~A;`), which iverilog simulates
# directly and verify_netlist.py evaluates independently.
#
# NOTE: the `abc -liberty nand.lib` route does NOT work with Yosys/ABC
# 0.33 — ABC rejects nand.lib ("Library with only 1 cell classes cannot
# be used": NAND2 and NAND2X have the same function, so ABC counts them
# as a single cell class). nand.lib is kept in the repo for reference;
# the -g NAND route below is the one that actually produces the netlist.
read_verilog release_logic.v
hierarchy -top release_logic
proc
opt
synth -noabc
abc -g NAND
clean
write_verilog -noattr release_logic_netlist.v
stat
